<title>USA: Hilton comfortable with pre-split estimate.</title>
<headline>Hilton comfortable with pre-split estimate.</headline>
<dateline>LAS VEGAS 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hilton Hotels Corp Chief Executive Officer Stephen Bollenbach said the company is comfortable with estimates it can earn $0.95 a share on a pre-split basis in the third quarter ended September 30.</p>
<p>&quot;We're comfortable with the market's expectations,&quot; Bollenbach told Reuters following a speech at the Salomon Brothers Gaming and Lodging Conference here, adding &quot;which is $0.95 a share, pre-split.&quot;</p>
<p>Under its purchase of Bally Entertainment Corp, Hilton set a four-for-one stock split. Analysts expect the company to earn $0.24 a share, post-split, according to First Call.</p>
